      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 309.08,
      "end_seconds": 339.67,
      "duration_seconds": 30.59,
      "text": "it's reasonable to be concerned, but right now plantar fasciitis is my leading thought, not anything worse let's book a foot X-ray to look into heel pain i'd rather check than guess, and this is the quickest way to know more i'd like you to take ibuprofen gel, three times a day, for two weeks it's for heel pain stretch the calf and the sole of the foot before getting out of bed and wear cushioned shoes"
